# This repo is edited on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) but runs on a Linux
# cluster. A shell script checked out with CRLF fails there with the very
# unhelpful:
#
#     bash: ./sbatch/submit.sh: /bin/bash^M: bad interpreter: No such file or directory
#
# Force LF in the working tree for everything that Linux has to execute or
# parse literally. Deliberately narrow: no blanket `* text=auto eol=lf`, which
# would rewrite every existing file's line endings and bury real diffs.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.sbatch  text eol=lf
*.slurm   text eol=lf

# Keep binaries out of any line-ending conversion.
*.pt      binary
*.pth     binary
*.ckpt    binary
*.npz     binary
*.npy     binary
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.pdf     binary
